    Add image embedding features with hand-crafted spatial extraction
    
    Adds 23 hand-crafted image features for datasets with image sidecar files.
    Features capture intensity statistics, quadrant patterns, center/edge
    contrast, brightness distribution, and color/saturation properties.
    
    Activation conditions:
    - Image files (.png, .jpg, .jpeg) detected in data subdirectories
    - PIL available
    - n_images >= 10
    
    Implementation details:
    - Filename pattern detection (regex-based) extracts linkage column values
    - Per-image computation using only PIL + numpy (no PyTorch dependency)
    - Signal detection via correlation with target after feature computation
    - Graceful failure: missing PIL, no images, or load errors all handled
    - Pipeline never crashes from image processing
    
    Verified on Award A (overdose epidemiology with MAT density heatmaps):
    - 8211 train + ~918 val PNG images at 256x256
    - Matched to (jurisdiction, period_id) via filename pattern
    - 100% match rate, 32 seconds total processing time
    - max_correlation_with_target = 0.106 (modest but real signal)
    - All 23 features integrated and used by model
    - Walk-forward MAE: 0.811 to 0.807 (0.5% improvement)
    - Strict CV MAE: 0.905 (unchanged)
    - No leakage, critic accepted
    
    Verified on retail (no images present):
    - Gracefully skips with skip_reason no_images_detected
    - Real test MAE: 9.04 (unchanged from baseline, no regression)
    
    CPU-friendly: under 10 minutes for 8000+ images.
    Cross-platform: uses only PIL + numpy from standard scientific stack.
    
    README updated to document image embedding capability.

